-- title:
--   Regularity of jmatĥ at the interior complex places
-- statement:
--   Fix $N \ge 1$ and write $F_N \subset \mathbb{Q}(\!(q)\!)$ for [`ModularCurve.modularFunctionFieldFull N`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L305), the intermediate field of the Laurent series field over $\mathbb{Q}$ generated by the set of series $\operatorname{qExpand}_{\mathbb{Q}} d\,(\hat\jmath)$ for the nonzero divisors $d \mid N$, where $\hat\jmath =$ [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) is the Laurent series $q^{-1}$ times the image of the integral power series `jNum` over $\mathbb{Q}$; and write $\mathbb{C}F_N$ for [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange ℂ F_N`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), the intermediate field of $\mathbb{C}(\!(q)\!)$ over $\mathbb{C}$ generated by the image of $F_N$ under the coefficientwise map `coeffEmb ℂ` induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to \mathbb{C}$. Let $D$ be a [`ModularCurve.ComplexPlaceDictionary N`](def/ModularCurve_ComplexPlaceDictionary.html#L28): data consisting of a map $\tau \mapsto D.\mathrm{pt}(\tau)$ from the upper half plane $\mathfrak{H}$ to places of $\mathbb{C}F_N$ over $\mathbb{C}$ (a valuation subring, proper, containing $\mathbb{C}$, and a principal ideal ring), a positive integer-valued ramification function, $\Gamma_0(N)$-invariance of $\mathrm{pt}$, the characterisation of membership in $D.\mathrm{pt}(\tau)$'s valuation subring by boundedness of $z \mapsto \|\operatorname{realize} N\,x\,z\|$ near $\tau$ with $z \ne \tau$, and the identity $\operatorname{meromorphicOrderAt}$ of the realization at $\tau$ $=$ ramification$(\tau)$ times $\operatorname{ord}_{D.\mathrm{pt}(\tau)}(x)$ for $x \neq 0$. Then for every $\tau \in \mathfrak{H}$, the element `coeffEmb ℂ jq` of $\mathbb{C}F_N$ lies in the valuation subring of $D.\mathrm{pt}(\tau)$.
--
--   This records that the modular invariant, viewed through its $q$-expansion as an element of the function field of $X_0(N)$ with complex coefficients, is regular at every place coming from a point of the upper half plane, the cuspidal places being the only poles. It is used in the analytic estimates on $j$ near the places of $X_0(N)$, in particular by [`ModularCurve.JZero.exists_log_secVal_sub_le`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JZero.exists_log_secVal_sub_le).
